# VoxelPort relay flags reference.
#
# The relay is configured entirely with command-line flags (see main.go) — there is
# no database and no separate admin API. This file documents the values baked into
# the systemd ExecStart line; edit that unit, not this file, to change them.
#
#   -listen    127.0.0.1:2526   WebSocket control + status listener (fronted by Caddy TLS)
#   -min-port  25500            lowest public Minecraft port assignable to a tunnel
#   -max-port  25999            highest public Minecraft port assignable to a tunnel
#
# Open TCP 25500-25999 in the VPS firewall — vanilla players connect to those ports
# directly at play.voxelport.in:<port>.
#
# To serve wss:// directly without Caddy, add:
#   -tls-cert /etc/voxelport/fullchain.pem  -tls-key /etc/voxelport/privkey.pem
# and bind -listen to a public address.
